    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0565" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115P44/32</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of the Counselor for the Department of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Polk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 19, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Baron Zwiedinek, Chargé of the Austrian Embassy, called and presented affidavits
                    of four seamen formerly employed on the steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Petrolite</hi>.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d368-f1"/> He pointed out that those
                    statements, which had been made by the men after they had read the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Petrolite</hi> note, were in conflict with some of the
                    facts stated in our note to the Austrian <pb facs="0566" n="280" xml:id="pg280"
                    /> Government on the subject of the <hi rendition="#italic">Petrolite</hi>. I
                    asked him to leave the affidavits with me and I would look them over. He said he
                    was on the point of sending a message to his Government but would hold it until
                    he saw me to-morrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rank</hi>] L. P[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">olk</hi>] </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
